  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Atlantic Diving Supply obligated $3B in FY2026 to date through federal contracts. Atlantic Diving Supply won 48,864 awards so far, with an average award size of $61.1K. Atlantic Diving Supply obligations are down 50.2% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows Atlantic Diving Supply obligations rose from $2.9B in FY21 to $6B in FY25, then moved to $3B in FY26. Atlantic Diving Supply receives the bulk of its federal money from the Department of Defense, which obligated $2.8B in FY2026 to date. Atlantic Diving Supply also has notable obligations from the General Services Administration, $84.4M, and smaller amounts from the Department of Homeland Security, $22.7M, and the Department of State, $21.2M. Atlantic Diving Supply sells across multiple NAICS markets, led by Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers at $1.7B and All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing at $871M. This profile summarizes where Atlantic Diving Supply is concentrated now and how that compares with recent fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Atlantic Diving Supply's top federal buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is Atlantic Diving Supply's top buyer, obligating $2.8B in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration follows with $84.4M. Other buyers include the Department of Homeland Security, $22.7M, and the Department of State, $21.2M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and products drive Atlantic Diving Supply's federal business?",
        "body": "Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers is Atlantic Diving Supply's largest market at $1.7B. All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing accounts for $871M, followed by Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing at $104M and All Other Miscellaneous Fabricated Metal Product Manufacturing at $61.6M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Atlantic Diving Supply make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Atlantic Diving Supply obligated $3B from federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Atlantic Diving Supply won 48,864 awards so far, with an average award size of $61.1K. Atlantic Diving Supply obligations are down 50.2% year over year. Historical obligations rose from $2.9B in FY21 to $6B in FY25 before reaching $3B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Atlantic Diving Supply?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is Atlantic Diving Supply's largest buyer, obligating $2.8B in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $84.4M. The Department of Homeland Security, the Department of State, and other agencies also buy from Atlantic Diving Supply, with obligations of $22.7M, $21.2M, and smaller amounts from other agencies."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Atlantic Diving Supply sell to the government?",
      "a": "Atlantic Diving Supply sells a mix of equipment and manufactured goods to the government, led by Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers at $1.7B and All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing at $871M. Atlantic Diving Supply also has obligations in Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing, $104M, and various apparel, medical, and metal product markets."
